{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>In Your wrath, do not [rebuke me]</b> — 'El [do not]' serves on account of what follows, and [similarly] 'in Your fury.' Like it: 'and the knowledge of the holy ones I shall <b>know</b>' [and] 'two commanders of troops were commanders of the son of Saul.'"], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 38, :notes {0 "The verse citation for 'ודעת קדושים אדע' is Numbers 24:16; 'שני שרי גדודים היו שרי' likely alludes to 1 Samuel (variously 13:17 or 14:2 context), where שרי functions as a cognate construction parallel to אל; the second example is textually compressed and the verse reference is inferred."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:30:06.828074024Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}